# The OTHER namespace. `extern "C"` lets the user pick the emitted C symbol
# outright, and the decode tested the emitted symbol — so binding an extern to
# `__callable_probe` had an ordinary `int` argument dereferenced as a
# `void*[2]` closure: SIGSEGV on the C lane with no diagnostic at all, and an
# `llc` type failure on LLVM.
#
# ⚠ BUILD-ONLY BY CONSTRUCTION: nothing in this program defines
# `__callable_probe`, so the correct outcome is a LINK failure naming the
# missing symbol — the same outcome any extern to an undefined symbol gets.
# There is no stdout to assert; the assertion is that the build fails HONESTLY
# instead of producing a binary that segfaults.
extern "C":
    extern int probe_add(int a, int b) = "__callable_probe"

void main():
    print(probe_add(40, 2))
